27:T863,{"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"FAQPage","mainEntity":[{"@type":"Question","name":"How many hours is Dammam to Jeddah by car?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Dammam to Jeddah is roughly 14 to 15 hours of driving for about 1,360 km, before stops. With rest, meals and prayers most trips take a full day and evening, which is why many travellers stay overnight in Riyadh."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Is there a taxi from Dammam to Jeddah?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Yes. We arrange a pre-booked private car with a driver from Dammam, Al Khobar or Dhahran to Jeddah. It is not a metered street taxi: you agree one fixed fare on WhatsApp before booking and the vehicle is yours for the whole trip."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"What does a private car from Dammam to Jeddah cost?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"The fare depends on the vehicle, the date and any overnight stop, so we quote each trip rather than publish a list. Send the details and we reply, usually within 1–2 hours, with a fixed fare. There is no meter and no surge."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Can the driver stop at the Miqat for Umrah?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Yes. Travellers coming from the east pass the Qarn al-Manazil Miqat at As-Sayl Al-Kabir, near Taif. Tell us when you book and the stop is planned into the trip."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Can you drop us at Jeddah airport instead of the city?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Yes. King Abdulaziz International Airport (JED) can be the drop-off. Share your flight time so the departure from Dammam is set with enough margin."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Can we go to Makkah or Madinah on the same trip?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Yes. Tell us the full plan in one message and we quote it as a single journey, including any waiting time and the onward leg."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"How do we pay?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Payment is by cash to the driver or by bank transfer, and an electronic receipt is available on request. Cancellation is free up to 24 hours before pickup."}}]}1c:["$","div",null,{"className":"min-h-screen bg-[#FAFAF7] pb-28 text-[#1C1C1C] lg:pb-16","children":[[["$","script","0",{"type":"application/ld+json","dangerouslySetInnerHTML":{"__html":"{\"@context\":\"https://schema.org\",\"@type\":\"Service\",\"name\":\"Dammam to Jeddah private transfer\",\"description\":\"Dammam to Jeddah by car is about 1,360 km and roughly 14 to 15 hours of driving through Riyadh and Taif. A private transfer gives you one vehicle and a driver for the whole trip, with rest and prayer stops, and the option of a night in Riyadh. Travellers going on to Makkah for Umrah pass the Qarn al-Manazil Miqat near Taif on this road. The fare is fixed and confirmed on WhatsApp before booking.\",\"serviceType\":\"Private intercity transfer\",\"url\":\"https://taxisaudiarabia.com/routes/dammam-to-jeddah\",\"provider\":{\"@id\":\"https://taxisaudiarabia.com/#taxiservice\"},\"areaServed\":[{\"@type\":\"Place\",\"name\":\"Dammam\"},{\"@type\":\"Place\",\"name\":\"Jeddah\"},{\"@type\":\"Place\",\"name\":\"Saudi Arabia\"}]}"}}],["$","script","1",{"type":"application/ld+json","dangerouslySetInnerHTML":{"__html":"$27"}}],["$","script","2",{"type":"application/ld+json","dangerouslySetInnerHTML":{"__html":"{\"@context\":\"https://schema.org\",\"@type\":\"WebPage\",\"@id\":\"https://taxisaudiarabia.com/routes/dammam-to-jeddah#webpage\",\"url\":\"https://taxisaudiarabia.com/routes/dammam-to-jeddah\",\"speakable\":{\"@type\":\"SpeakableSpecification\",\"cssSelector\":[\"h1\",\"#speakable-summary\"]}}"}}]],"$L28","$L29","$L2a","$L2b"]}]
