33:["$","p",null,{"className":"mt-6 rounded-2xl bg-[#F0FDF4] p-4 text-sm leading-relaxed text-[#166534]","children":"Distance is the measured road distance and driving time is an estimate. Traffic, weather and stops change the real time, so we plan your pickup with margin and never promise an exact arrival minute."}]
34:["$","section",null,{"aria-labelledby":"sr-tradeoff","className":"rounded-3xl border border-[#16A34A]/15 bg-white p-6 sm:p-8","children":[["$","h2",null,{"id":"sr-tradeoff","className":"font-heading flex items-center gap-2 text-2xl font-bold","children":[["$","$L2d",null,{"ref":"$undefined","iconNode":[["path",{"d":"M12 3v18","key":"108xh3"}],["path",{"d":"m19 8 3 8a5 5 0 0 1-6 0zV7","key":"zcdpyk"}],["path",{"d":"M3 7h1a17 17 0 0 0 8-2 17 17 0 0 0 8 2h1","key":"1yorad"}],["path",{"d":"m5 8 3 8a5 5 0 0 1-6 0zV7","key":"eua70x"}],["path",{"d":"M7 21h10","key":"1b0cd5"}]],"className":"lucide-scale h-5 w-5 text-[#16A34A]","aria-hidden":true}]," ","Dammam to Jeddah: by car, by plane or by train?"]}],["$","div",null,{"className":"mt-3 space-y-3 text-[0.95rem] leading-relaxed text-[#475569]","style":{"maxWidth":"70ch"},"children":[["$","p","There is no direct train from Dammam to Jeddah. The railway from Dammam ends in Riyadh, and the Haramain line on the west coast is a separate network, so a rail trip still leaves the long Riyadh to Jeddah section to cover another way.",{"children":"There is no direct train from Dammam to Jeddah. The railway from Dammam ends in Riyadh, and the Haramain line on the west coast is a separate network, so a rail trip still leaves the long Riyadh to Jeddah section to cover another way."}],["$","p","Flying is the fastest option and is the right one for most solo and business travellers; we can arrange the airport transfers at both ends. A private car is the better fit when you are a family with a lot of luggage, when you want to stop in Riyadh or Taif, when you are combining the trip with Umrah, or when someone in the group prefers not to fly.",{"children":"Flying is the fastest option and is the right one for most solo and business travellers; we can arrange the airport transfers at both ends. A private car is the better fit when you are a family with a lot of luggage, when you want to stop in Riyadh or Taif, when you are combining the trip with Umrah, or when someone in the group prefers not to fly."}],["$","p","Driving yourself is possible, but it is two long days at the wheel. With a private transfer the driver handles the road, and you agree one fare for the vehicle before you leave.",{"children":"Driving yourself is possible, but it is two long days at the wheel. With a private transfer the driver handles the road, and you agree one fare for the vehicle before you leave."}]]}]]}]
